    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1109">

                <pb facs="0928" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/4007.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-25T01:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 25, 1912—1 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>If you believe the letter to be really from Zapata, and representing his real
                    intentions, immediately inform President Madero, in strict confidence. Also tell
                    the Defense Committee of the Society of the American Colony quickly and quietly
                    to circulate the news among all Americans so that if the attack is made they may
                    gather at the selected concentration points, where the American flag should be
                    flown. No reply should be made to Zapata. No part should be taken by Americans
                    in disorders unless urgently necessary for self-protection. Use your discretion
                    in informing other foreign colonies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
